From b4142c97de3f58ecd0ad165f7589c001017ebdd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prateek <palprateek2004@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 01:55:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(ai): send OpenCode client identity to satisfy
 free-tier gate (#12306)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OpenCode Zen/Go gate the contributor free tier on client identity: a
User-Agent whose leading token is opencode/<version> and an
x-opencode-session matching ses_<12 hex><14 alnum>. omp's omp/* UA and
raw session/install ids failed both checks, producing 403 FreeTierError
on every free-tier model.

applyInferenceHeaders now sends the canonical OpenCode UA and a stable
ses_ token derived from the conversation session id (routing and prompt
cache stay pinned across turns); conversation-less background traffic
(usage polls, model discovery) attributes through the same formatter
with the install id. The shared formatter lives in
packages/catalog/src/wire/opencode.ts so catalog discovery and pi-ai
send identical identity. Explicit caller UA overrides (Claude OAuth
fingerprint) still win.

