From 713e154db9f6210b9f2edef634db4f93ad7b1c00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prateek <palprateek2004@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 02:37:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(ai): satisfy OpenCode free-tier body gate and scope
 its 403 denial
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The #12306 gate is body-shaped as well as header-shaped: it requires
stream:true and at least five OpenCode core tool names (bash, edit,
glob, grep, read) in tools[], so tool-less auxiliary calls (advisors,
one-shot helpers) were still refused with 403 FreeTierError after the
client-identity fix. stream() now pads such requests with stub entries
for the missing names via withOpenCodeGateTools — empty description,
inert {type:"object"} schema, strict:false — wire-shape filler that
never joins the caller's tool registry. Agent rosters that already
carry the names pass through untouched (same array identity).

When a denial does surface, isOpencodeFreeTierGateMessage classifies
it as model-scoped client policy rather than a credential fault: the
key keeps serving paid SKUs, so the 403 no longer rotates sibling
credentials (isAuthRetryableError and stream()'s rotatable-403 arm) or
reads as an auth failure, and formatMessage rewrites the raw 403 into
an explanation that preserves the classifier markers. google-shared
now passes provider into finalize() so the zen google-transport lane
gets the same treatment.

